	   ***  tAo  PARAMETERS FILE  ***
	       (default unities : I.S.)


PARAMETER	CORRESPONDING 		USE
 VALUES		  VARIABLES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Gridding:
501 		nx		Number of x points (distance).
201		nz		Number of z points (depth for rheological calculations).

Limits:
0		x0		Modelizated x range.
1e6		xf

Window:
100e3		xmin		Limits of the output window.
900e3		xmax
-8000		ymin
1000		ymax


Lithosph. geometry:
30000		espelastdefault	Default ET (if no .EET file) 
32000		espcortdefault	Default crustal geometry for gravity anomaly
15000		espcortsup 	 and rheological calculations when no .CRUST and .UCRUST
0		altmedidaanom 	Height of gravity anomaly measuring (0 for Bouguer anomaly)
-3000		alt0 		Altitude of  the initial plate position from sea level.


Densities:
3300		densmanto	Mantle.
2900		denscort	Crust (just for anomaly calculation).
2800		densinfill	Infilling material (only when switch_topoest=1).
2300		denssedim	Sediments.
0		densamb		Air (or water for oceanic flexure), 


Erosion model parameters:
2e8		Kerosdif, 	Diffusive erosion constant.
.2		Keroseol, 	Continental background erosion rate constant.
10		Ksedim, 	Water sedimentation constant.
2e2		maxprofsed	Max. water thickness contributing to sedimentation.



Time variables [Ma]:
0		Timeini		Initial time.
20		Timefinal	Final time.
5		tau		Relaxation time.
1		dt		Increment time.
5		dtmemounit	Time elapsed between units recording. 
				  if = 0 only file-defined load units will be recorded. 


Boundary Conditions:
3		boundary_conds	#0: Continuous simetric half-plate.
				#1: Broken plate (left).
				#2: Continuous plate.
				#3: Free ends.
				#4: Hunging plate.
				#5: Broken plate (right).

External forces:
0e12		tecforce	Horizontal tectonic force (compressive if >0).
0e12		appshearforce	Applied force as bound. cond. in case 1. (left side).
0e17		appmoment 	Torque as bound. cond. case 1. (left side).


0	switch_rheolimit & lith_type	
				To switch rheological calculations:
				#1: for oceanic lithosphere
				#2: for continental.
				#0: no rheol. calc.: Pure elastic or
					viscoelastic model


These are switches to turn on options of the model.
Their possible values are 1 (yes) or 0 (no):
0	switch_viscoelast	For viscoelastic model.
0	switch_topoestable	For load to stay without moving.
1	switch_mar		For existence of sea.
1	switch_erosed		For erosional-deositional model.
0	switch_calcanom		For gravity anomaly calculation.
0	switch_compactar	For compacting(not available).

i/o switches:
1	switch_write_file	For file output.
1	switch_ps		For postscript output.
0	switch_output		For graphic output(PV-WAVE).
0	switch_verbose		For more runtime prints.
0	switch_debug		For more runtime prints.

v3.2	version			Release


(END OF PARAMETERS FILE)

Comments:
    This is a tAo 3.2 parameter file. 
	--You can modify the format of this parameter files, by adding more 
  comment lines or changing comments in the existing lines after the values.
  Comment lines cannot start with a number.
	--You can run the simplest model (without any load file *.CRG) just 
  varying the b.c. parameters 'appshearforce' & 'appmoment' and the 'tecforce'
  external horizontal force. 
	--Default unities: I.S.  (except indication).
	--If  (switch_topoestable != 0) then the load will rest at zero level 
  and plate subsidence will be filled with 'densinfill' material. Do not use 
  with erosion model.
	--'tecforce' is compressive if >0.
	--You can get more information about the meaning of each parameter in 
  the tao.h file and tao.info file.

